  "helpFaqDataSafeTitle": "Is my data safe?",
  "@helpFaqDataSafeTitle": {"description": "Title on the Help and support page (faq card)."},
  "helpFaqDataSafeBody": "Yes. SSH, SFTP, FTPS and Mosh sessions are encrypted between this device and your server. Telnet is not: it sends everything as plain text. Your passwords and keys are kept on this device and leave it only when you choose: Cloud Sync and team vaults carry them encrypted so that ZestSSH cannot read them, a backup is encrypted with your password unless you export without one, and a host you share can come with its saved password.",
  "@helpFaqDataSafeBody": {"description": "Message text on the Help and support page (faq card)."},
  "helpFaqDataCollectTitle": "What data do you collect?",
  "@helpFaqDataCollectTitle": {"description": "Title on the Help and support page (faq card)."},
  "helpFaqDataCollectBody": "ZestSSH has no analytics, telemetry or crash reporting. We do not track what you connect to, what commands you run, or how you use the app. ZestSSH Cloud keeps only what running it needs, and the libraries for purchases and sign-in send some device details to their makers: the privacy policy names each.",
  "@helpFaqDataCollectBody": {"description": "Message text on the Help and support page (faq card)."},
  "helpFaqCloudSyncTitle": "How does Cloud Sync work?",
  "@helpFaqCloudSyncTitle": {"description": "Title on the Help and support page (faq card)."},
  "helpFaqCloudSyncBody": "Cloud Sync encrypts your hosts, keys, and passwords on-device using a password you set (Argon2id key derivation + AES-256-GCM). The encrypted blob is uploaded to our server. We cannot read your data: only you can decrypt it with your sync password.",
  "@helpFaqCloudSyncBody": {"description": "Message text on the Help and support page (faq card)."},
  "helpFaqSshSecurityTitle": "What SSH security is supported?",
  "@helpFaqSshSecurityTitle": {"description": "Title on the Help and support page (faq card)."},
  "helpFaqSshSecurityBody": "ZestSSH supports Ed25519, ECDSA, and RSA keys. Connections use modern ciphers (ChaCha20-Poly1305, AES-GCM, AES-CTR). Host key verification uses a Trust-On-First-Use (TOFU) model with a local known_hosts database.",
  "@helpFaqSshSecurityBody": {"description": "Message text on the Help and support page (faq card)."},
  "helpFaqPasswordsTitle": "Where are my passwords stored?",
  "@helpFaqPasswordsTitle": {"description": "Title on the Help and support page (faq card)."},
  "helpFaqPasswordsBody": "Passwords and private key passphrases are kept in your platform's secure storage (Android Keystore / iOS Keychain / Windows Credential Manager / macOS Keychain). The app writes them to a file as plain text only when you ask for it: an export without a password. A session log or transcript that you save as plain text keeps what the terminal showed.",
  "@helpFaqPasswordsBody": {"description": "Message text on the Help and support page (faq card)."},
  "helpFaqDeleteAccountTitle": "How do I delete my account?",
  "@helpFaqDeleteAccountTitle": {"description": "Title on the Help and support page (faq card)."},
  "helpFaqDeleteAccountBody": "Open your Account page and choose Delete account. After you sign in again, ZestSSH Cloud removes your account and what it keeps for you at once: your synced data and your keys. They leave the server's backups within 6 weeks. Purchase records are kept for accounting, and what you added to a team stays with the team. After a reset of cloud sync, the account can be deleted once the 30 days that keep the old copy are over. Data on your devices stays until you remove it.",
  "@helpFaqDeleteAccountBody": {"description": "Message text on the Help and support page (faq card)."},
  "helpFaqOpenSourceTitle": "Is ZestSSH open source?",
  "@helpFaqOpenSourceTitle": {"description": "Title on the Help and support page (faq card)."},
  "helpFaqOpenSourceBody": "ZestSSH's SSH engine, zest_ssh_core, is open source under the MIT license: a fork of the open-source dartssh2 project. From version 4.0 the app's own source code is published too. The Open source licenses page in About lists every part of the app with its license.",
  "@helpFaqOpenSourceBody": {"description": "Message text on the Help and support page (faq card)."},
  "helpFaqImportTitle": "Can I import SSH configs?",
  "@helpFaqImportTitle": {"description": "Title on the Help and support page (faq card)."},
  "helpFaqImportBody": "Yes. Go to Hosts → Import hosts and select your ~/.ssh/config file. ZestSSH will parse Host entries and create a host for each one, including proxy jumps and the key files they name (IdentityFile).",
  "@helpFaqImportBody": {"description": "Message text on the Help and support page (faq card)."},
  "helpFaqTiersTitle": "What are the tiers?",
  "@helpFaqTiersTitle": {"description": "Title on the Help and support page (faq card)."},
  "helpFaqTiersBody": "Free: {desktop, plural, =1{1 session} other{{desktop} sessions}} on desktop and {mobile} on mobile, unlimited hosts, SSH, SFTP, port forwarding, snippets, keys, and sync to your own storage. Squeezed ($9.99, one-time): unlimited sessions, jump hosts, automation, custom themes, and more. Juiced ($24.99, one-time): hosted ZestSSH Cloud storage for sync on up to 7 devices, so you need not run your own backend. Bundle ($29.99): both together. Each is bought once, with no subscription. Teams buy seats once as well; only Business, which adds company sign-in, is a subscription.",
  "helpVersionInfo": "ZestSSH v{version} ({buildNumber})",
  "@helpVersionInfo": {
    "description": "Text on the Help and support page (footer). {version} is a version number. {buildNumber} is the build number.",
    "placeholders": {
      "version": {
        "type": "String"
      },
      "buildNumber": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
