  "@profileSignInNotReadTitle": {"description": "Notice title on a Mac: the sign-in in the keychain read as nobody, or could not be read, and nobody signed out. The data stays open."},
  "profileSignInNotReadBody": "ZestSSH could not read your sign-in on this Mac, so you are not signed in right now. Your data here stays open as it was, and nothing was locked or deleted. Sign in again with the same account to keep syncing.",
  "@profileSignInNotReadBody": {"description": "Body of profileSignInNotReadTitle. An error code follows it."},
  "profileSignInUnreadBody": "macOS did not let ZestSSH read your sign-in from the keychain, so you are not signed in right now. Your data here stays open as it was, and nothing was locked or deleted. Choose Try again, then Always Allow, and type your Mac login password.",
  "@profileSignInUnreadBody": {"description": "Body of profileSignInNotReadTitle where macOS did not let the app read the sign-in from the keychain (a no, or no answer). Try again is macKeychainTryAgain; Always Allow is the button in macOS's own question (use macOS's own word for it in the language). An error code follows it."},
  "profileLockedTitle": "Your account's data is locked",
