  "@desktopShellTelnetReopenTabs": {"placeholders": {"hosts": {"type": "String"}}, "description": "First sentence of the red Unencrypted connection question when the app, as it starts, would bring back tabs of the last run that are Telnet hosts. {hosts} is their names, comma separated. Cancel is the dialog's Cancel button: the other tabs come back, the Telnet ones do not. The sentences 'Use SSH instead whenever possible. Continue with Telnet?' follow it."},
  "desktopShellTelnetInWorkspace": "This workspace includes Telnet: {hosts}. Cancel opens its other panes only.",
  "@desktopShellTelnetInWorkspace": {"placeholders": {"hosts": {"type": "String"}}, "description": "First sentence of the red Unencrypted connection question when a saved workspace that is being opened has panes on Telnet hosts. {hosts} is their names, comma separated. Cancel is the dialog's Cancel button: the other panes open, the Telnet ones stay empty. The sentences 'Use SSH instead whenever possible. Continue with Telnet?' follow it."},
  "certLifetimeOutageNote": "While ZestSSH Cloud cannot be reached, members cannot get a new certificate. The one they hold works until it ends, and an owner can hand one over as a QR code or text.",
  "@certLifetimeOutageNote": {"description": "Help under 'Each certificate lasts' in a vault's certificate settings (owners), after certLifetimeHelp. Says what a short lifetime means while ZestSSH Cloud is unreachable: members' requests for a new certificate travel through it, so they cannot get one; an owner can hand one over directly (Certificate from an owner)."},
  "orchardRulesOfflineOutageCounts": "Time during which ZestSSH Cloud itself is down counts too. An owner can sign a pass that lifts the limit on a device for up to {days} days.",
  "@orchardRulesOfflineOutageCounts": {"placeholders": {"days": {"type": "int"}}, "description": "Said where a team's or a vault's offline limit is set, in a build that cannot have an outage of ZestSSH Cloud proven to it (no status service; the opposite of orchardRulesOfflineOutageNote). The limit counts from the device's last contact, so an outage of ZestSSH Cloud itself counts. A pass is the offline pass an owner signs (vaultUiPassHelp). {days} is the longest a pass lasts, 7."},
  "vaultUiWatchedOnAway": "While ZestSSH Cloud cannot be reached nobody can be asked to watch. Owners then connect after giving a reason; everyone else waits, unless you allow them to connect as well.",
  "@vaultUiWatchedOnAway": {"description": "One point of the question an owner answers before sessions to a vault's hosts are watched. Says what happens while ZestSSH Cloud is unreachable: watching needs it, so only owners connect (after giving a reason) unless the owners allow the others too (the vault's 'unwatched while ZestSSH Cloud is away' switch)."},
